{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head implementation artifact at stable path docs/reference/architecture.md for the custody lost-update repair, answering ratified changes-requested report #10113. Head e2326e2446702c9cd772f42cbba73bcb8cd4f892 on branch request/custody-lost-update (worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/custody-lost-update) distinguishes the four custody paths the architecture page conflated: raw SaveConfig publishes a first configuration by hard link; Unix UpdateConfig holds an exclusive advisory lock on .config.lock across one whole load-modify-store, reloading from disk so stale memory cannot erase another process's custody; platforms without advisory locking refuse updates loudly while first creation stays available; and the workspace's in-memory configuration lock is process-local snapshot consistency, distinct from persisted cross-process custody. Companion exact-head artifacts already published at internal/app (#10398) and internal/apphost (#10402). Gates actually run on this head: gofmt -l . clean (exit 0); go vet ./... exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; GOOS=windows go build ./... exit 0; go test -race ./internal/app/... ./internal/apphost/... ./internal/custody/... -count=1 exit 0 (all ok); go test ./... -count=1 exits 1 only in internal/docset TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord, a pre-existing world-moved citation flare on pages naming retired events with named successors, unrelated to this head's changes and covered by separately queued re-anchoring work.","body":{"branch":"request/custody-lost-update","commit":"e2326e2446702c9cd772f42cbba73bcb8cd4f892","head":"e2326e2446702c9cd772f42cbba73bcb8cd4f892","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}